# cppcheck accepted baseline for Static Chaos (issue #62).
# High-value checks stay ACTIVE (buffer overflow, array-index OOB, error-severity
# null deref, format/scanf issues, uninit) so new bugs fail CI. Only these
# known-intentional idioms / heuristic noise are muted:
uselessAssignmentPtrArg      # Merc `arg = one_argument(arg, x)` idiom: the reassigned local cursor IS used after
nullPointerRedundantCheck    # legacy over/under-defensive null checks; not deref bugs
AssignmentIntegerToAddress   # 32-bit int<->pointer, intentional -- this build is -m32 (see docs/TOOLCHAIN.md)
CastIntegerToAddressAtReturn # ditto (32-bit int<->pointer)
toomanyconfigs               # informational only
# comm.c login/send paths: `ch` is established non-null by the loader/caller invariant
# (file-scoped so nullPointer stays active everywhere else).
nullPointer:src/comm.c
